ve, Abraham gave gifts to the sons of his concubines and sent them away from his son Isaac to the land of the east.","from":48},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Rachel died and was buried on the way to Ephrath (that is, Bethlehem).","from":51},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Reuben, you are my firstborn, my might, and the beginning of my strength, excelling in honor, excelling in power.","from":42},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":22,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then tell Pharaoh that this is what the LORD says: ‘Israel is My firstborn son, and I told you to let My son go so that he may worship Me. But since you have refused to let him go, behold, I will kill your firstborn son!’”","from":42},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From the hilltop the border curved to the spring of the Waters of Nephtoah, proceeded to the cities of Mount Ephron, and then bent around toward Baalah (that is, Kiriath-jearim).","from":50},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Ziph, Telem, Bealoth,","from":42}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}